  "body": "The [Beacon API](http://www.w3.org/TR/beacon/) adds a new feature to the platform — non-Service-Worker requests that outlive their document — but adds it in a high-level API with a narrow use-case (and poorly defined delivery, which is nether at-most-once, nor at-least-once).\n\nThere is no [lower-level primitive in that \"explains\"](https://extensiblewebmanifesto.org/) the Beacon API. Perhaps `fetch` could be it? \n\n```\nfunction sendBeacon(url, body) {\n    fetch(url, {\n        method: 'post',\n        body,\n        detachedFromDocumentLifetime: !!\"bikeshed\",\n        keepRetryingInUnspecifiedManner: \"like the beacon spec\",\n        ageHeaderUpdatedOnRetry: 'Beacon-Age',\n    });\n}\n```\n",
